    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0917" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v14/pg889"/>

                <head>471. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Israel<anchor n="1" xml:id="d471-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-12-29T14:33:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                                1955—2:33 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>445. Please convey to FonMin text following
                    message from Secretary: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dear Mr. Minister: I received your letter of December 12 just as I was
                            departing for Paris. With regard to request of the Israel Government for
                            purchase of arms in this country, which you mention, Mr.Allen informed Ambassador Eban on December 13<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d471-f2"/> that we were unable reach decision this time for
                            number of reasons, prominent among them being recent incident on Syrian
                            border.</p>
                        <p>“In your letter you also give Israel Government’s views with respect to
                            some of questions involved in an Arab-Israel settlement. I hope the
                            Israel Government will continue to give its most careful consideration
                            to solution at this time of the various issues between Israel and her
                            Arab neighbors. I am convinced that a resolution of this conflict would
                            be of the greatest benefit to Israel and go far to remove a threat that
                            otherwise must be of the gravest concern to all who are interested in
                            its welfare.</p>
                        <p>“With kindest personal regards, sincerely yours,John Foster Dulles.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Signed original enroute Tel Aviv by pouch.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d471-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
